{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/940569-gifmalu-igizalag-the-explorer-2e","id":940569,"title":"Gifmalu Igizalag, The Explorer (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T04:35:45-07:00","id":940569,"title":"Gifmalu Igizalag, The Explorer (2E)","content":"The so-called Mad Scientist is hardly a Victor Frankenstein, puttering away at a bolt-necked giant in a hidden castle at a distant remove. Instead, it hides in the nooks and crannies of the Uratha\u2019s territories, creating twisted monstrosities of spirit and flesh. And unlike the Intelligent Designer of human myth, the idigam seems to have no greater plan. Its work has all the forethought of child\u2019s play in a sandbox.<br /> <br /> Gifmalu Igizalag takes a profound joy in altering its own form. It may appear as a cylindrical column, an angular structure, a silver snake or even, on rare occasions, a humanoid figure. Its preferred form seems to be crablike; its body flattens into a rigid disk and it protrudes between six and 14 jointed legs that end in knife-like blades. This form always includes at least two arms with fine manipulators (such as fingers). Sometimes this form has recognizable perception organs, such as eye stalks or a human face, jutting from the front of the entity (if it can be said to have a front); other times, it may have no discernible eyes, instead sprouting silver tentacles or spines about the edges of its disklike body. In all forms, the idigam retains its monochrome silver color.<br /> <br /> [For more information on this Idigam, see p. 143 of Night Horrors: Wolfsbane]<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Gifmalu Igizalag, The Explorer</b></u><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 10, Finesse 15, Resistance 11<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Envy 2, Flesh 3<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/824054-2e-conversion-numina\">Camouflage</a>, Dement, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/824054-2e-conversion-numina\">Dessication</a>, Drain, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/824054-2e-conversion-numina\">Gauntlet Vision</a>, Innocuous, Rapture, Regeneration*, Sever Fetter, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/824054-2e-conversion-numina\">Versatile Energies</a><br /> <b>Essence Shaping:</b> Essence Trap, Ghost Manipulation, Forge Servant (Claimed, Flesh-Bound Spirit), Locus Manipulation, One Million Eyes, Spirit Manipulation<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Divine Clay, Pierce Mind, Purification, Shifting, Swift<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 16<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 100<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 35 (Species Factor 10)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 26<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Living human beings (mortal or supernatural) burned within 100 yards of the idigam. Each point of damage they suffer inflicts a point of damage on its Corpus.<br /> <br /> * Gifmalu Igizalag can spend Essence to heal two points of bashing damage or one point of lethal damage per point of Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:37:10-07:00","id":940571,"title":"","content":"2E Conversion of another Night Horrors Idigam. <i>Zul Sanak</i> is now next on my list.<br /> <br /> I'm still stumped over what kind of Ban I should give the Explorer, since the 1E Ban made more sense as a Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}